{title: 569 - Pass Me Not, O Gentle Savior}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #569 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 569}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Pass me [C]not, O gentle [G]Savior,
[D7]Hear my [G]hum[D7]ble [G]cry;
[G]While on [C]others Thou art [G]calling,
[D7]Do not [G]pass [D7]me [G]by.
[G]Savior, [C]Savior, [G]hear my humble [D]cry;
[G]While on [C]others Thou art [G]calling,
[D7]Do not [G]pass [D7]me [G]by.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[G]Savior, Savior, [C]hear my [G]humble cry;
[D7]while [G]on others [D7]thou [G]art calling,
[G]do [C]not pass [G]me by.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Let me [C]at thy [G]throne of mercy
[D7]find [G]a [D7]sweet [G]relief,
[G]kneeling [C]there in [G]deep contrition;
[D7][G]help [D7]my [G]unbelief.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Trusting [C]only in [G]thy merit,
[D7]would [G]I [D7]seek [G]thy face;
[G]heal [C]my wounded, [G]broken spirit,
[D7]save [G]me [D7]by [G]thy grace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Thou the [C]spring of [G]all my comfort,
[D7]more [G]than [D7]life [G]to me,
[G]whom have [C]I on [G]earth beside thee?
[D7]Whom [G]in [D7]heaven [G]but thee?
{end_of_verse}
